SUMMARY:Author Talk: Karin A. Martin - Get Plum Island!
LOCATION:Boston Public Library\, 700 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA 02116
DESCRIPTION:Join University of Michigan professor Karin A. Martin for a con
 versation about her new book Get Plum Island!: Place and Politics in Massa
 chusetts’s Ten-Year Fight Over the Parker River National Wildlife Refuge
 . The book tells the story of how the USFWS became interested in establish
 ing a national wildlife refuge in Massachusetts\, why Essex County became 
 a premiere location\, and how local communities and the state nearly succe
 eded in having the refuge abolished. Instead\, after rounds of Congression
 al hearings and pocket veto by President Truman\, a compromise was reached
 \, reducing the refuge to about half its original size\, and yet preservin
 g the wonderful\, vibrant refuge we know today.\nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons
 .com/events/6ab28390101eb7003f320c4c\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin
 .city/boston/
URL:https://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ab28390101eb7003f320c4c
END:VEVENT
