SUMMARY:Quabbin—Yesterday and Today
LOCATION:Hyde Park Library
DESCRIPTION:through Nov 30\nThis exhibit contrasts the Quabbin Reservoir wh
 en it was built in the 1930s with what it has become today. It was recentl
 y featured at the Massachusetts State House and is now going on the road t
 o libraries in the communities that receive their water from the Quabbin\,
  to help raise awareness about the sacrifices it took to build the Quabbin
  as well as the impact of climate change upon their water supply.\nhttps:/
 /bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ac52fbd96ec3a003ad8a73d\nFrom Pushpin Bosto
 n: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ac52fbd96ec3a003ad8a73d
